# III. Main Dashboard Data & Lists

## Top of Main View
- Reserve top area for important page actions or simple navigation (e.g. "Create" button, filter dropdown via `AdminPopover`).

## List Item Anatomy (Keep Simple)
Each list item should include where applicable:
- Thumbnail/favicon (visual identification — product image, order icon)
- Primary label (shortened identifier)
- Secondary meta (destination, customer, SKU)
- Creation date
- Count/metric (clicks, quantity, revenue)
- Brief description (GitHub-style one-liner)

## Visual Separation
- Do **not** give each item its own full border — causes clutter.
- Stack into clean lists using **space**, **subtle dividers** (`divide-y`), or **alternating row colors**.

## Empty States
- Always design a deliberate `EmptyState` with graphic/prompt and CTA when no data exists.

## Micro-interactions (Bulk Actions)
- Allow users to **check/select multiple items**.
- Instantly trigger a contextual **`BulkActionsBar`** when ≥1 item is selected.

## Tables
- Use `DataTableShell` with search, filter, and sort.
- Tables are useless without interactivity — always provide search/filter/sort.

## Implementation
- Use `AdminList`, `AdminListItem`, `DataTableShell`, `EmptyState` from layout components.
